## Why This Is Asked
Tests for CMS publish workflows require coordinating multiple roles, specific state transitions, and data integrity. A beginner-friendly scenario introduces test orchestration, data seeding, and timing-sensitive assertions in a realistic, multi-tenant setting.

## Key Concepts
- End-to-end flow with multiple roles and explicit state transitions
- Data seeding and test isolation across tenants
- Latency mocking and retry-based visibility checks

## Code Example
```javascript
// Cypress sketch
cy.request('POST', '/seed', { users, articles, tenants });
cy.login('writer');
cy.get('#new-article').type('Hello');
cy.click('Save Draft');
cy.login('reviewer');
cy.approve('article-id');
cy.login('publisher');
cy.publish('article-id');
cy.visitPublicFeed();
cy.contains('Hello').should('be.visible');
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify audit log integrity for failed publishes?
- How would you scale this to parallelize multiple article publishes without cross-test interference?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design realistic E2E checkout scenarios under network stress, locale shifts, and stock race conditions. It validates understanding of deterministic mocks, proper data isolation, and robust failure handling.

## Key Concepts
- End-to-end data seeding with deterministic mocks
- Real-time UI updates across viewports
- Locale and region switching with discount persistence
- Race conditions: stock changes during checkout
- Failure handling, rollback mechanisms, and idempotency

## Code Example
```javascript
// Playwright E2E skeleton
test('checkout with promo code', async ({ page }) => {
  await seedTestData({ locale: 'en-US', promo: 'SAVE20' });
  await page.goto('/cart');

  // Apply promo code
  await page.getByLabel('Promo Code').fill('SAVE20');
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Apply' }).click();

  // Verify discount applied
  await expect(page.locator('.discount')).toHaveText('-$20.00');
  await expect(page.locator('.total')).toHaveText('$80.00');

  // Mobile viewport
  await page.setViewportSize({ width: 375, height: 812 });
  await expect(page.locator('.total')).toHaveText('$80.00');

  // Switch locale
  await page.getByLabel('Language').selectOption('de-DE');
  await expect(page.locator('.discount')).toHaveText('-€18,00');

  // Checkout with stock race condition
  await page.goto('/checkout');
  await mockInventoryDecrement();
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Pay' }).click();
  await expect(page.locator('.error')).toContainText('insufficient stock');
});
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes concrete E2E strategies for feature flags in multi-tenant, latency-sensitive systems, ensuring isolation, observability, and fast rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Feature flags, canary rollout, rollback semantics
- Multi-tenant data isolation and tenant-scoped routing
- End-to-end with API mocks, network latency, and analytics verification
- Cross-browser/mobile coverage

## Code Example
```javascript
// Playwright snippet (conceptual)
test('feature-flag canary rollout', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.route('**/api/flags/**', route => route.fulfill({ status: 200, body: JSON.stringify({ flag: true }) }));
  // navigate to onboarding
  await page.goto('/onboarding');
  // assert canary UI visible only when flag on
  const el = page.locator('#instant-onboard');
  await expect(el).toBeVisible();
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you expand this to test concurrent flag changes during peak load?
- How do you ensure no cross-tenant data leakage when the flag toggles?

## Why This Is Asked
Offline-first reliability with service workers is a critical requirement in modern e-commerce applications. This question evaluates whether a candidate understands how to test caching behavior, connectivity state changes, and retry logic in end-to-end tests.

## Key Concepts
- Offline-first UX patterns with service workers
- Network throttling and failure simulation (Cypress or Playwright network interception)
- Test data isolation with fixtures or unique identifiers
- Idempotent order placement to prevent duplicate charges

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: Intercept network requests to simulate offline behavior
cy.intercept('POST', '/api/payment', (req) => {
  req.reply({ statusCode: 503, body: { error: 'Network error' } });
}).as('paymentRequest');

// Simulate going offline
cy.networkIdle(); // or use Cypress offline plugin
cy.window().then((win) => {
  win.navigator.onLine = false;
});

// Verify offline UI and localStorage persistence
cy.get('[data-testid=offline-banner]').should('be.visible');
cy.getLocalStorage('cart').should('exist');

// Restore network and retry
cy.networkOn();
cy.wait('@paymentRequest').then(() => {
  cy.get('[data-testid=order-confirmation]').should('be.visible');
});

// Verify idempotent order creation
cy.get('@paymentRequest').its('response.statusCode').should('eq', 200);
```

